# Intent: The grid games end on the shared game-over screen (UX15, docs/design/game-over-screen.md) instead of a banner and a three second hold: a face (amber and smiling for a win, blue and sad for a loss, gray and level for a draw) that pops for 160 ms, the result, the game's score line ("Score 38", "Cleared in 82 s", "Length 31", "The word was robot"), the best line or the amber "New best!" mark, and Play again and Quit buttons of 148 by 56 px. Play again starts the same game fresh, Quit returns to the games page; the screen waits for a tap (a minute with none ends the game). The result sounds stay (the fanfare, the soft fall, the neutral draw) and a new best adds the ting. The data-pack games (Color Memory, Whack-a-mole, Tic-Tac-Toe, Do It, Rock Paper Scissors, the eight ball, dice) keep their own ending until their result table is wired.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal (ours)
# Check after a flash: finish a Four in a Row game: the game-over screen shows with the right face and the score and best lines; tapping Play again starts a fresh board, Quit shows the games page; a new best shows the New best! mark and rings; the swipe down from the grabber still ends the game from the screen.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_GAMES (existing)
# Memory cost: about 15 LVGL objects while the screen shows (freed with the game); no PSRAM; a few hundred bytes of flash.

